Bluetooth Phone Recorder
========================

The code in src/, tools/, tests/ and scripts/ is under the BSD 3-Clause
licence (see LICENSE).

The program includes BTstack (third_party/btstack, git submodule, release
v1.8.3), Copyright (C) BlueKitchen GmbH. BTstack's licence is BSD-style with
one extra condition:

    4. Any redistribution, use, or modification is done solely for personal
       benefit and not for any commercial purpose or for monetary gain.

Because the built program contains BTstack, the program as a whole may only
be used, shared and modified for non-commercial purposes. This extra
condition is also why the project is not GPL: the GPL does not allow added
restrictions, so GPL code cannot be combined with BTstack. For commercial use,
BlueKitchen sells licences: https://bluekitchen-gmbh.com

BTstack itself bundles:
  - Bluedroid SBC codec (Apache 2.0)
  - Google LC3 codec (Apache 2.0)
  - tinydir (BSD 2-Clause)

Libraries used from the system (not shipped): GTK 4 and libadwaita (LGPL 2.1+),
PipeWire (MIT), libusb (LGPL 2.1+), libsndfile (LGPL 2.1+), speexdsp (BSD),
zstd (BSD), xz/liblzma (0BSD), libsoup 3 and json-glib (LGPL 2.1+).

Bluetooth firmware is never shipped. It is read from the system's
/lib/firmware (linux-firmware package) and unpacked into the user's cache.
